'''''Aphelinus asychis''''' is a parasitoid wasp native to Eurasia that was introduced to [[North America]] to control the [[Russian wheat aphid]].<ref>{{cite journal | author = Hopper, K.R. | author2 = Cutinot, D. | author3 = Chen, K. | author4 = Halbert, S.E. | author5 = Kazmer, D.J. | author6 = Mercadier, G. | author7 = Miller, R.H. | author8 = Pike, K.S. | author9 = Tanigoshi, L.K. | name-list-style = amp | year = 1996 | title = Exploration for natural enemies to control Diuraphis noxia in the United States. | journal = Symposia Proceedings of the Entomological Society of America, Lanham, MD.}}</ref> It has six different aphid hosts, including ''[[Acyrthosiphon pisum]]''.<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Jia |first1=Yu-Jie |last2=Wang |first2=Bo |last3=Liu |first3=Tong-Xian |title=Unsuccessful Host Stinging by Aphelinus asychis (Hymenoptera: Aphelinidae) Impacts Population Parameters of the Pea Aphid (Hemiptera: Aphididae) |journal=Journal of Economic Entomology |date=6 June 2020 |volume=113 |issue=3 |pages=1211–1220 |doi=10.1093/jee/toaa025 |pmid=32112092 |url=https://academic.oup.com/jee/article/113/3/1211/5766676?searchresult=1 |access-date=30 December 2022|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

Recent work shows that the species as currently described does not form a monophyletic group and its taxonomy and phylogenetic relationship should be re-examined.<ref>{{cite journal|author1=Yu Cheng Zhu |author2=Quentin Q. Fang |title=The phylogenetic relationships of introduced ''Aphelinus'' (Hymenoptera: Aphelinidae), biological control agents of the Russian wheat aphid (Homoptera: Aphididae) |journal=Insect Science |year=2009 |volume=16 |issue=3 |pages=277–285 |doi=10.1111/j.1744-7917.2009.01249.x |doi-access=free |bibcode=2009InsSc..16..277Z }}</ref>

